# XSH qsort() and qsort_r()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The sort is not required to be stable, so elements that compare equal may
# come out in any order. The comparison function may be given pointers to
# the array or to copies of elements, so only the values it is shown are
# checked, never where they live.

assertion  XSH.qsort.001
anchor     functions/qsort.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       qsort() puts int arrays in ascending order: random data, already
           sorted, reversed, all equal, and with few distinct values, for
           1, 2, 3, 10, 1000 and 50000 elements, and the result is a
           permutation of the original values.
test       t/001-ascending.c

assertion  XSH.qsort.002
anchor     functions/qsort.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       Elements of 12 bytes (a key and 8 bytes derived from it) are moved
           whole: after qsort() every record is intact, the keys are
           ascending and every original record is still present once.
test       t/002-records.c

assertion  XSH.qsort.003
anchor     functions/qsort.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       With nel zero the comparison function is not called and the array
           is left as it was.
test       t/003-empty.c

assertion  XSH.qsort.004
anchor     functions/qsort.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       The order is the one the comparison function defines: a descending
           comparison gives a descending array, and an array of string
           pointers sorted with strcmp() is in strcmp() order.
test       t/004-order.c

assertion  XSH.qsort.005
anchor     functions/qsort.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       qsort_r() passes its arg pointer, unchanged, as the third argument
           of every call to the comparison function, and sorts as the
           comparison function directs (the context flag selects ascending
           or descending).
test       t/005-qsort-r.c

assertion  XSH.qsort.006
anchor     functions/qsort.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       With nel zero qsort_r() does not call the comparison function.
test       t/006-qsort-r-empty.c
